! C22-6578 PROBLEM 2.8, "PURCHASING LIST ARITHMETIC", printed pp.20-21
! (PDF 21-22), read in the ink (and at 170 dpi).
!
! >>> REGISTERED 2026-11-16 AS PRINTED, AND THE PRINTED PROGRAM IS WRONG:
! >>> IT CANNOT LEAVE THE KOMF LOOP.  The model is right; the card is not.
! >>> Run with ASM=strap2, stopped deliberately at the 40th arrival at KOMF
! >>> (half-word 2020).  The card the program meant: problem_2_8_komf8.strap;
! >>> with the signed ADD corrected too: problem_2_8_corrected.strap.  <<<
!
! WHERE IT ERRS: "KOMF  KF(BU,24)(V+I), 0.8($2)" -- the field length.
! TRACED INSTRUCTION BY INSTRUCTION ON THE MODEL 2026-11-16 (a per-clock
! display of the counter, X1, X2, the accumulator and word 11):
!  * LCV leaves count 3 in $L; three decimal adds of E; the two (V+I)
!    stores leave X2's value at 1203.48, product 1's G; M+ makes $FT 36.
!  * "L(BU, 32), TESTW" leaves the accumulator's low 32 bits E N D
!    (11111111) = (16)354733FF (IQS E=35, N=47, D=33).
!  * "KF(BU,24),0($2),8" compares G's first three bytes, 49 41 FF ("OK"
!    and product 2's A mark), with the accumulator field ending 8 bits from
!    its right end, E N D: AL, not AE, so no branch to LAST.  Right.
!  * KOMF compares three bytes at X2 with the three-byte accumulator field
!    at offset 0, which is N D (11111111) = 4733FF, then adds 0.8 to X2.
!    Observed: 49 41 FF -> AL; 41 FF 01 -> AH; FF 01 02 -> AL; ... every
!    pass AL or AH (word 11 bits 60, 62), never AE (61), each the unsigned
!    24-bit order of the bytes; X2 walks on past product 2's END
!    (1208.40 at the 40th arrival) and the loop never ends.
! The reading is the Reference Manual's: KF compares "a field in the
! accumulator ... the same length in bytes as the field from storage
! exclusive of the sign byte, and its location is specified by the offset
! in the usual manner" (printed p.65, PDF 68); the offset "specifies the
! number of bits by which the right end of the accumulator operand is
! offset from the right end of the accumulator" (printed p.56, PDF 59); in
! progressive indexing "the value field ... is used as the effective
! address ... Subsequent to this use ... the address part ... is added to
! the value field" (printed p.21, PDF 24).
! WHY NO DATA RESCUES THE PRINTED CARD: KOMF then MORE ("V+I, $2, 1.0") must
! leave X2 on the next D field, 72 bits past that product's all-ones mark A
! (A 8 + B 16 + C 48).  A one-byte compare matching at A does: X2 = A+8,
! +64 = A+72 -- the printed comment "bypass 64 more bits to new D field".
! The printed three-byte field can match only a window N D (11111111),
! i.e. one starting at A-16, which leaves X2 at A-8 and MORE at A+56,
! sixteen bits short of D; and even that needs a G ending in "ND".  No
! window within this list matches (TESTW itself holds 4733FF, outside it).
! So the printed (BU,24) should be (BU,8), and the test of comment (b),
! "Note the KF's cannot be replaced by simple K operations", fits that: a
! K would bring E N D into a one-byte compare.
!
! THE PRE-RUN HAND TRACE (docs/NEXT.md, G2.3) predicted a halt with F2 = 8
! and $FT = (16)404.  It was wrong about THIS card -- it took KOMF to stop at
! the mark -- and right about everything else: problem_2_8_komf8.strap,
! which changes only this card, halts with exactly F2 = 8, $FT = (16)404.
!
! WHAT THE STOPPED RUN PINS (words the loop cannot move): F1 = 36 (word
! 1203 = (16)0000000003064941: "+(D,48,8)" is signed, so E's last byte is
! read as a sign byte and E is +00012, added three times); product 2's F
! never written (word 1207 as loaded); $FT = (16)36 packed; $RM 0.
!
! DISCRIMINATING: with the decimal ADD reading its field unsigned (injected
! 2026-11-16), this run FAILS F1 (03 07 05) and $FT ((16)375); with KF's
! accumulator field taken at offset 0 whatever the offset, it still passes
! -- that injection is caught by problem_2_8_komf8 and _corrected
! (tests/run_tests.sh has the failure sets).
!
! A SIDE OBSERVATION, NOT PINNED: the decimal "+" adds E to the whole
! accumulator, and LCV left the BINARY count 3 in $L's bits 0-17 (16)C in a
! digit position.  The add rewrites it ($L (16)0000C000... becomes
! (16)00012000...) -- the open "invalid digit met by an add" item of
! docs/NEXT.md G2.3.  F and $FT do not depend on it.
!
! THE TWO BLANK F SUBFIELDS were one "(IQSQ)DD(BU,96,8)" each until
! 2026-11-16; STRAP II refuses it ("FIELD LENGTH GREATER THAN 64",
! C22-6531's limit), so each is two 48-bit DDs.  Same bits; the data are
! the deck's, not the page's.
!
!   "A purchasing list consists of a string of fields, each of which
!   has the following structure:  | A | B | C | D | E | F | G |
!   Subfield A is an eight-bit byte consisting of 1's.
!   Subfield B has two 8-bit bytes (item no.).
!   Subfield C has six 8-bit bytes (coded name of product).
!   Subfield D has three 8-bit bytes, and contains the number of units
!     of the product desired in decimal (DU, 24, 8).
!   Subfield E has six 8-bit bytes, and contains the unit price in
!     cents of the product in decimal (DU, 48, 8).
!   Subfield F has 12 8-bit bytes, and is blank (to be the total price
!     field).
!   Subfield G is an unknown number of 8-bit bytes.  It contains the
!     remarks concerning the product and/or the entire purchase.  The
!     first three 8-bit bytes of the subfield G in the last "product
!     field" contains the 8-bit IQS expression END.  None of the 8-bit
!     bytes in G are all 1's.
!   If the complete string begins at LIST, write a program to fill in
!   the total price for each product in (DU, "96", 8).  For simplicity
!   of programming do repeated additions instead of decimal
!   multiplications.  Create the grand total also, and put it (DU,
!   "128", 8) in the pseudo accumulator 13.0 through 14.0 ($RM and
!   $FT)."
!
! THE PRINTED STATEMENTS are START to XW2 below, as printed, except:
!
!  * THE PAGE PRINTS THE LABEL "LCON" TWICE, on "LX, $2, XW2" and on
!    the LCV under it, and "B, LCON" at the end of the loop.  The loop
!    must return to the LCV (returning to the LX would start the list
!    again), so the second is LCON2 here and the branch is B, LCON2.
!    That is the deck's reading; the ink has LCON on both lines.
!  * ' comments are written !'.
!
! READINGS WORTH RECORDING:
!  * "128-18" is right, and is the same device as Problem 2.7's -18:
!    the converted count's last bit lands in bit 17 of $L, and LOAD
!    COUNT takes "bits 0-17 of the half-word" (Reference Manual printed
!    p.24).
!  * "+(D, 48, 8)" is printed SIGNED, though E is described (DU, 48,
!    8).  Not resolved here.
!  * "(IQSQ)DD(DU,24,8),ENDQ": Q closes the alphabetic field; comment
!    (d) is about the blanks.
!
! THE DATA is the deck's: two products, 3 at 125 cents and 2 at 40.
! FROM THE PROBLEM STATEMENT the totals are 375 and 80 cents and the
! grand total 455 -- which problem_2_8_corrected.strap gets, digits one a
! byte with zone 0000.
!
! A SECOND REASON IT CANNOT RUN ON THIS ASSEMBLER: strap_asm assembles
! "DD(DU,48,8), 000125" as the BINARY integer 125, not as six decimal
! digit bytes.  That is an assembler finding with its own reproducer,
! repro_dd_decimal_mode.strap, and a section in docs/NEXT.md.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   Z, $FT
LCON    LX, $2, XW2
LCON2   LCV(DU, 24, 8)(V+I), 0.24+0.48($2),128-18    !'$R cleared too
        LC, $1, $L; BXCZ, NEXT                       !'binary count field
ADD     +(D, 48, 8),-0.48($2)
        CB, $1, ADD
NEXT    ST(DU, 64, 8) (V+I), 0.64($2), 16            !'store total into F
        ST(DU, 32, 8) (V+I), 0.32($2)
        M+(DU, 64, 4), $FT                           !'update grand total
        L(BU, 32), TESTW
        KF(BU, 24), 0($2),8                          !'test for end of string
        BAE, LAST
KOMF    KF(BU,24)(V+I), 0.8($2)                      !'test for beginning of new field
        BZAE, KOMF
MORE    V+I, $2, 1.0                                 !'bypass 64 more bits to new D field
        B, LCON2
LAST    L(DU, 64, 4), $FT
        ST(DU, 64, 8), $FT
        ST(DU, 64, 8), $RM, 64
HALT    BEW, $
TESTW   (IQSQ)DD(DU,24,8),ENDQ                       !'end mark for string
        DD(BU, 8, 8), (2)11111111                    !'beginning mark for field
XW2     XW, LIST+0.72, 0, $

        SLC, 1200.0
! product 1: item 07, "BOLTS ", 3 units at 000125 cents, remarks "OK"
LIST    DD(BU, 8, 8), (2)11111111
        DD(DU,16,8), 07
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),BOLTS Q
        DD(DU,24,8), 003
        DD(DU,48,8), 000125
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,16,8),OKQ
! product 2: item 12, "NUTS  ", 2 units at 000040 cents, remarks "END"
        DD(BU, 8, 8), (2)11111111
        DD(DU,16,8), 12
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),NUTS  Q
        DD(DU,24,8), 002
        DD(DU,48,8), 000040
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(BU,48,8),      Q
        (IQSQ)DD(DU,24,8),ENDQ
        END, START
